                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What GST applies to software services in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Domestic IT services: 18% GST under SAC 9983. Export: zero-rated via LUT (Form RFD-11). Export invoices in GSTR-1 Table 6A as 'without payment of tax'. ITC on domestic inputs (rent, cloud, office) claimable even for zero-rated. Patron handles LUT and Table 6A for Mumbai IT exporters.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How does LUT work for Mumbai software exporters?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Filed annually in Form RFD-11, valid one FY (April-March). Invoice foreign clients at zero GST without IGST. Mention LUT ARN on invoices. FIRC/e-FIRA collected for every export receipt. Patron files each April and tracks FIRC realisation.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does IT company accounting cost in Mumbai?</h3>
